Note: for primes the finite-size law is BELOW 1/sqrt2 (0.69 at E = 2*10^4) because of the 1/sqrt(ln E) factor;
it converges to 1/sqrt2 from below like sqrt(ln E / ln 2E).  For primes the Roth-Szekeres law log p(E) ~ 2 pi sqrt(E/(3 ln E)) has beta = 1/2 with a log
correction; the law f(2h)/(2f(h)) -> 1/sqrt2 regardless of the log factor.  Squares: Hardy-Ramanujan
log p_sq(E) ~ 3 (pi/4)^{1/3} zeta(3/2)^{2/3} E^{1/3} / ln 2 ; the finite-E law is above 2^{-2/3} = 0.630.
